---
kind: lore
id: north.cinderMansionTrainers
title: Cinder Mansion trainers
---

// The trainers haunting the burned mansion (the key hand-off is the scene
// north.cinderMansion). Repeat visits get the creaking-house entry.

<entry id="northMansionAgain" on="enterPlace" target="place.cinderMansion" category="bark" priority="-1">
  @narrator: The mansion creaks. The study is empty now, and the burned portraits watch you go past.
</entry>

<beat use="trainerBattle" id="cinderMansionBurglarSly" who="cinderMansionBurglarSly" intro="This house burned down with a fortune in it. I've been looking for a year. You're not taking my fortune!" win="I'll find it one day. Probably under a floorboard." lose="Finders keepers!" prize="2000"/>

<entry id="northSlyAfter" on="talk" target="npc.cinderMansionBurglarSly" category="bark" when="holds(defeated(cinderMansionBurglarSly))">
  @cinderMansionBurglarSly: A year in here and all I've found is a spoon and an Eclipse badge somebody dropped. Recently.
</entry>

<beat use="trainerBattle" id="cinderMansionScientistHale" who="cinderMansionScientistHale" intro="This lab made history! Then it burned it. I'm here for the notes, and you're in the way!" win="The notes survived. My team didn't." lose="Science prevails!" prize="2200"/>

<entry id="northHaleAfter" on="talk" target="npc.cinderMansionScientistHale" category="bark" when="holds(defeated(cinderMansionScientistHale))">
  @cinderMansionScientistHale: Men in black came here last month and took every page they could find. They missed the ones in the iron box. Amateurs.
</entry>

<beat use="trainerBattle" id="cinderMansionBurglarNip" when="@isNight" who="cinderMansionBurglarNip" intro="Nobody comes here after dark! Except me. And now you. That's too many!" win="Okay. You can stay. I'll go." lose="Night belongs to burglars!" prize="2000"/>

<entry id="northNipAfter" on="talk" target="npc.cinderMansionBurglarNip" category="bark" when="holds(defeated(cinderMansionBurglarNip))">
  @cinderMansionBurglarNip: I only work nights. In daylight the portraits look at you.
</entry>
